android: W2 — WLR_X11_SOCKET_DIR for X11 lock/socket filesystem paths

Android has no /tmp. open_display_sockets() creates /tmp/.X<n>-lock and
binds the filesystem socket under /tmp/.X11-unix — every display number
fails ENOENT → "No display available in the first 33" → gamescope's
Xwayland server creation dies (fatal).

WLR_X11_SOCKET_DIR redirects the filesystem artifacts (lock files, socket
dir, filesystem socket). The ABSTRACT socket name stays the standard
/tmp/.X11-unix/X%d — kernel namespace, no fs, and X11 clients connect
to it by that exact name. The GameNative launcher sets
WLR_X11_SOCKET_DIR=<imagefs>/tmp and pre-creates <dir>/.X11-unix
(0700, owned by us → check_socket_dir passes).

socket_fmt2 (non-linux second-socket suffix) folded away: the fs socket
path now always comes from the env base; non-linux keeps the /tmp
default. Xwayland never binds sockets itself (wlroots passes -listenfd).

